{
  "about": "The schema language's own findings in a pass over a complete document or a layer (SCHEMA-5, SCHEMA-7, SCHEMA-9, SCHEMA-12, SCHEMA-13, SCHEMA-15, EXPR-7, VALUE-1, TIME-10, LAYER-4, LAYER-9, WINDOW-1). Each case's schema is one module, schema.yaml, whose entry class is root_class. `schema_document` reads a complete document as an author wrote it, a list member named by the text of its `name` or `id` and otherwise by a rendering of what it holds; `schema_layer` reads a layer, inside each member of a keyed collection (`input`, `windows`, `columns`, `rows`, `intermediates`) as a fragment whose requiredness waits for the resolved specification. A case that names both operations states that a fragment reports what the complete document reports. A case compares a complete list where its source stated every finding, and otherwise finds each finding by its cause among those the pass reports; its rows compare phase, condition, rule and path, with the context or the `expected` of the context where its source stated them. A value that fails a descriptor's values, pattern and minimum length reports exactly those three findings, in the order constraints are checked (values, pattern, minimum length, then exact size). The rows from the Rust tests of schema_validation.rs and schema_references.rs keep those tests' paths, conditions and context; each phase is the registry's (yaml/conditions.yaml) and each rule the one the cause cites in the condition table. A class validated by itself (schema_types), which no version gates, reports its missing required field, a field of the wrong type and an unknown field in that order, each with its context, names a list member by its index, and admits an int field's integer beyond 64 bits as written; these rows are declaration_schema_capture.rs's, whose tests read the class from a captured schema and the document from YAML.",
